JB-2.03a — the eyedropper's pill hit test, the ring's place in the view order, and the recent-colours
rule, for the owner of JoyBrushActivity.kt to apply.

Written by the JB-2.03a audit-fix pass, which does not edit this file (LEAD_DESK rule 3: it is Lead-owned,
and another lane is holding it). Apply AFTER that lane has landed, together with
JbCanvasView_JB-2.03a-audit.patch, which adds the `onStrokeCommitted` this file's last hunk uses:

    git apply tasks/joybrush/held/JoyBrushActivity_JB-2.03a-audit.patch

HUNKS 1 AND 2 together move the ring above the chrome. Today `root.addView(ring, ...)` sits before the
reference, the guides and the tool strip, so a ring under the strip is a ring nobody can see — and the
finger's own ring, lifted 76 dp above a fingertip near the bottom of the screen, is exactly there. The
ring is drawn last instead, under the 2 dp hairline, which is the app's own rule and stays on top of
everything. The trade: for the second or two the eyedropper is up, its ring is over an open popover.
That is the owner's call, not mine.

HUNK 4 is the pill's own hit test. `ev.x <= v.width` counts a point one pixel past the last column of the
swatch as being on it, and a pick that should be taken is thrown away. The rule is Eyedropper.overPill
and EyedropperTest.thePillHitTestStopsOnePixelBeforeTheEdge pins it; the two call sites at 1419 and 1424
do not change.

HUNK 3 moves the recents push off `onStrokeEnded` and onto `onStrokeCommitted`. `onStrokeEnded` fires for
a CANCELLED stroke as well, and a long-press that becomes the eyedropper cancels its stroke (R26 makes
that signal the save queue's release, so it must not be narrowed), which put a colour in the bar that had
never painted anything. D.02c Decision 3: a colour joins the history when a stroke is FINISHED with it.
Nothing in this file or the canvas can be tested off-device, so this one is a device check: long-press and
lift, and the recent-colours bar must not grow.

